# TOE Agda corpus handoff

This is the complete Agda corpus available in this checkout at handoff time.
It contains the RH/analytic lane only. The two copies are intentionally
preserved: `Agda-reference/` is the selected handoff layout and
`Agda/DASHI/Analysis/` is the repository-style layout.

## Intake instruction

Treat this archive as a source corpus and provenance input for the TOE sewing
pass. Do not import every file into the TOE kernel. First index each module,
its imports, declarations, status, and any Lean mirror. Then classify every
candidate correspondence as exactly one of:

* `exactInstance`
* `approximateInstance`
* `finiteShadow`
* `structuralAnalogue`
* `candidateBridge`
* `negativeResult`
* `openSocket`

The corpus index should record source path, module name, domain, PR/branch
status when known, theorem shape, proposed TOE owner, validation status, and
claim boundary. Keep merged code, open-PR material, source-only Agda, and Lean
re-proofs distinct. Similar names or prose are not evidence of a bridge.

## Suggested TOE owners to test

Check these surfaces against the existing owners, without silently discharging
their hypotheses:

* `FiniteReindex`: centered grids, finite retention, and Gram/determinant
  invariance;
* `StructureMorphism`: Poisson/channel transport and commuting-square claims;
* `CertifiedMargin`: coercivity, retained defect, envelope and contraction
  gates;
* `PathTransport`: source transport and reachability-shaped statements;
* `ResidualTaxonomy`: discarded tails, off-diagonal terms, and normalization
  defects;
* `ObserverBundle` / `MultiscaleDescent`: analytic source-to-observer layers;
* `CommutatorObservability`: only if a genuine path-order distinction and an
  observation map are supplied.

For each proposed bridge, ask: does the map commute; does the observable
descend; what residual is required; what symmetry survives; and what is the
coarsest sufficient observation level? Record `yes`, `no`, `conditional`, or
`open`, including the exact missing hypothesis.

## Validation and boundaries

No Agda toolchain was available when this archive was prepared. Do not report
the Agda modules as typechecked. Lean mirrors, where present in the wider
project, are separate evidence and must not be treated as automatic proofs of
the Agda source. This bundle makes no claim about RH, zeta zeros, physics, a
mass gap, or a theory of everything.

Do not add Yang--Mills or Navier--Stokes material from unrelated archives. Keep
negative results and open sockets in the corpus index: the goal is a complete
constraint map, not a catalogue of only successful analogies.

